-- title:
--   Twisted centraliser of a diagonal δ with distinct norms
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Let $v$ be a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, write $K_v$ for the completion and $E_v = L \otimes_K K_v$, and let $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E_v)$ have vanishing off-diagonal entries, with the $K_v$-algebra norms of its two diagonal entries distinct. Let $a \neq b$ in $K_v$ and let $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ have matrix $\mathrm{diag}(a,b)$. The assertion is twofold. First, the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser $\{t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E_v) : t\,\delta\,\sigma(t)^{-1} = \delta\}$, where $\sigma$ acts entrywise, equals the image under the entrywise map $\iota : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(E_v)$ induced by $x \mapsto 1 \otimes x$ of the centraliser of $\{\gamma\}$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$. Second, both subgroups being given their Borel $\sigma$-algebras, for every Haar measure $\tau'$ on the twisted centraliser there is a Haar measure $\tau$ on the centraliser of $\gamma$ whose pushforward along $\iota$ agrees, as a measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(E_v)$ with its Borel $\sigma$-algebra, with the pushforward of $\tau'$ along the inclusion.
--
--   This identifies the local $\sigma$-twisted centraliser occurring in Langlands' base change for $\mathrm{GL}(2)$, in the regular split case, with the base change of the diagonal torus over $K_v$, and records that Haar measures match up under this identification. It supplies the measure-transport input to the bound on twisted orbital integrals against indicators of semi-local integral sets.
